  "lines": [
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "6 SPQR: Great Battles of the",
      "x0": 45.2,
      "top": 25.053600000000074,
      "x1": 306.0,
      "bottom": 36.35820000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "cent Numidian light cavalry. They rarely carried any armor,",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 54.003600000000006,
      "x1": 297.1170000000002,
      "bottom": 64.0036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "other than a shield, or any other weapon.",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 66.0036,
      "x1": 208.02000000000004,
      "bottom": 76.0036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "Lancers: Essentially light cavalry units trained to",
      "x0": 90.5,
      "top": 83.4036000000001,
      "x1": 297.00199999999995,
      "bottom": 93.4036000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "use a lance for attack. They have no missile capabil-",
      "x0": 90.5,
      "top": 95.4036000000001,
      "x1": 297.0,
      "bottom": 105.4036000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "ity (a simplification for game purposes).",
      "x0": 90.5,
      "top": 107.4036000000001,
      "x1": 251.04000000000005,
      "bottom": 117.4036000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "Heavy Cavalry: Cavalry with some body armor,",
      "x0": 90.5567,
      "top": 128.80360000000007,
      "x1": 297.04870000000005,
      "bottom": 138.80360000000007
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "light shields and, perhaps, a lance and/or sword. The",
      "x0": 90.4967,
      "top": 140.80360000000007,
      "x1": 297.0167,
      "bottom": 150.80360000000007
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "heavy cavalry of the day was descended from Alex-",
      "x0": 90.4967,
      "top": 152.80360000000007,
      "x1": 297.00270000000006,
      "bottom": 162.80360000000007
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "ander’s Companions, although they were nowhere",
      "x0": 90.4967,
      "top": 164.80360000000007,
      "x1": 297.0037,
      "bottom": 174.80360000000007
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "near as effective.",
      "x0": 44.996700000000004,
      "top": 176.80360000000007,
      "x1": 112.83170000000001,
      "bottom": 186.80360000000007
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "Roman Cavalry: The Roman cavalry, including that",
      "x0": 90.4598,
      "top": 194.20360000000005,
      "x1": 297.06679999999994,
      "bottom": 204.20360000000005
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "of the alae, was in terms of weapons and armament,",
      "x0": 90.49980000000001,
      "top": 206.20360000000005,
      "x1": 297.0268,
      "bottom": 216.20360000000005
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "more heavy than light in that they copied much from",
      "x0": 90.49980000000001,
      "top": 218.20360000000005,
      "x1": 297.00379999999996,
      "bottom": 228.20360000000005
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "the Greek era. However, they were neither trained in,",
      "x0": 90.49980000000001,
      "top": 230.20360000000005,
      "x1": 297.03479999999996,
      "bottom": 240.20360000000005
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "nor especially adept at, Shock Combat on the same level as",
      "x0": 44.99980000000001,
      "top": 242.20360000000005,
      "x1": 297.1157999999999,
      "bottom": 252.20360000000005
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "“Heavy” cavalry, so they have received a different designation",
      "x0": 44.99980000000001,
      "top": 254.20360000000005,
      "x1": 297.0097999999999,
      "bottom": 264.20360000000005
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "and a separate line on the Shock Superiority Chart, although they",
      "x0": 44.99980000000001,
      "top": 266.20360000000005,
      "x1": 297.0197999999998,
      "bottom": 276.20360000000005
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "are treated as HC on the Clash of Spears and Swords Chart. The",
      "x0": 44.99980000000001,
      "top": 278.20360000000005,
      "x1": 297.0058000000001,
      "bottom": 288.2036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "Romans never quite understood how to use cavalry and, although",
      "x0": 44.99980000000001,
      "top": 290.2036,
      "x1": 297.01480000000004,
      "bottom": 300.2036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "they often had large numbers, they were rarely as effective as",
      "x0": 44.99980000000001,
      "top": 302.2036,
      "x1": 296.9847999999998,
      "bottom": 312.2036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "one would expect.",
      "x0": 44.99980000000001,
      "top": 314.2036,
      "x1": 118.03980000000001,
      "bottom": 324.2036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "Elephants: By this time, the sight of elephants on a",
      "x0": 90.5,
      "top": 331.6036,
      "x1": 296.9980000000001,
      "bottom": 341.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "battlefield was common—to everybody, that is, ex-",
      "x0": 90.5,
      "top": 343.6036,
      "x1": 297.00199999999995,
      "bottom": 353.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "cept the Romans. Alexander’s descendants, the Di-",
      "x0": 90.5,
      "top": 355.6036,
      "x1": 297.00499999999994,
      "bottom": 365.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "adochi, had fallen in love with them, and a trained",
      "x0": 90.5,
      "top": 367.6036,
      "x1": 297.018,
      "bottom": 377.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "elephant corps was standard throughout the wars of Ptolemy,",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 379.6036,
      "x1": 297.0059999999999,
      "bottom": 389.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "Seleucus, etc. The Romans, however, had not yet encountered",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 391.6036,
      "x1": 297.0149999999999,
      "bottom": 401.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "them when Pyrrhus arrived with his 20+ behemoths at Heraclea.",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 403.6036,
      "x1": 297.00699999999995,
      "bottom": 413.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "The result was typical: the Roman cavalry had a collective",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 415.6036,
      "x1": 297.1400000000001,
      "bottom": 425.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "coronary, and the Roman infantry didn’t wait around long enough",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 427.6036,
      "x1": 296.86699999999973,
      "bottom": 437.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "to see their EKGs. By the time of Hannibal, however, the Romans",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 439.6036,
      "x1": 297.10700000000037,
      "bottom": 449.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "were pretty much used to them and had devised some ingenious",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 451.6036,
      "x1": 297.0199999999999,
      "bottom": 461.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "methods of negating their abilities; the effectiveness of jousting",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 463.6036,
      "x1": 297.00299999999993,
      "bottom": 473.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "chariots and the flaming pigs of the Pyrrhic era having proved",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 475.6036,
      "x1": 297.00099999999986,
      "bottom": 485.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "rather elusive. The elephants of Hannibal were the smaller, North",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 487.6036,
      "x1": 296.87999999999977,
      "bottom": 497.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "African forest variety—not the big Indian tuskers that Porus had",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 499.6036,
      "x1": 297.006,
      "bottom": 509.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "at the Hydaspes (or, for that matter, the much larger southern",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 511.6036,
      "x1": 296.9979999999999,
      "bottom": 521.6035999999999
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "African variety)—and were usually equipped with towers, pur-",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 523.6035999999999,
      "x1": 297.0,
      "bottom": 533.6035999999999
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "portedly an invention of Pyrrhus. Pyrrhus’ elephants, inherited",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 535.6035999999999,
      "x1": 297.0169999999998,
      "bottom": 545.6035999999999
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "from the Diadochi, were probably the bigger, Indian variety. War",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 547.6035999999999,
      "x1": 297.0489999999998,
      "bottom": 557.6035999999999
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "elephants were pretty much impervious to anything—except",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 559.6035999999999,
      "x1": 296.8799999999998,
      "bottom": 569.6035999999999
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "sharp, pointy objects and loud, strange noises. They also tended",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 571.6035999999999,
      "x1": 297.00199999999995,
      "bottom": 581.6035999999999
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "to have a mind of their own when annoyed, which often happened",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 583.6035999999999,
      "x1": 297.02499999999975,
      "bottom": 593.6035999999999
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "when confronted with those same sharp, pointy objects and",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 595.6035999999999,
      "x1": 296.9500000000001,
      "bottom": 605.6035999999999
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "strange sounds.",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 607.6035999999999,
      "x1": 106.66,
      "bottom": 617.6035999999999
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "Scorpio: A Scorpio was a small, catapult-like engine",
      "x0": 90.4,
      "top": 625.0036,
      "x1": 297.01100000000014,
      "bottom": 635.0036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "that was something like a crossbow on a tripod. It could",
      "x0": 90.5,
      "top": 637.0036,
      "x1": 296.89000000000016,
      "bottom": 647.0036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "shoot a large, spear-like bolt about 300-400 yards. The",
      "x0": 90.5,
      "top": 649.0036,
      "x1": 297.01099999999997,
      "bottom": 659.0036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "“artillery” was fairly standard issue to legions, and it",
      "x0": 90.5,
      "top": 661.0036,
      "x1": 296.9999999999999,
      "bottom": 671.0036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "was used almost entirely for camp defense (the size, range and use",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 673.0036,
      "x1": 297.03500000000025,
      "bottom": 683.0036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "of these early artillery pieces is open to much debate).",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 685.0036,
      "x1": 255.55999999999986,
      "bottom": 695.0036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "© 2026 GMT",
      "x0": 263.9613,
      "top": 750.0107,
      "x1": 306.0,
      "bottom": 758.0107
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "e Roman Republic – 5th Ed.",
      "x0": 306.0,
      "top": 27.35820000000001,
      "x1": 404.26030000000003,
      "bottom": 36.35820000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "2.5 GAME SCALE",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 53.81099999999992,
      "x1": 413.34000000000003,
      "bottom": 65.81099999999992
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "Each hex is approximately 70+ paces (yards) from side to side.",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 69.197,
      "x1": 566.973,
      "bottom": 79.197
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "Each game turn covers about 20 minutes of real time.",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 81.197,
      "x1": 528.8499999999999,
      "bottom": 91.197
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "Each point of Size denotes from 100-150 infantry (depending on",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 98.59699999999998,
      "x1": 567.011,
      "bottom": 108.59699999999998
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "their formation, rank depth and usage) or 100 cavalry. Thus, an",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 110.59699999999998,
      "x1": 567.0139999999999,
      "bottom": 120.59699999999998
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "African Phalanx unit represents 1500+ men, a Roman Principes",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 122.59699999999998,
      "x1": 567.0029999999999,
      "bottom": 132.59699999999998
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "unit 300, and a Roman Heavy Cavalry unit about 300 men. Each",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 134.59699999999998,
      "x1": 567.0069999999998,
      "bottom": 144.59699999999998
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "Roman legion infantry unit is the equivalent of 2–3 maniples",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 146.59699999999998,
      "x1": 567.015,
      "bottom": 156.59699999999998
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "(granted, that’s an unwieldy division of labor; however, it makes",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 158.59699999999998,
      "x1": 566.9339999999997,
      "bottom": 168.59699999999998
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "frontages realistic and, more importantly, the game playable).",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 170.59699999999998,
      "x1": 567.0129999999999,
      "bottom": 180.59699999999998
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "Skirmishers are an exception; their size reflects not their numeri-",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 182.59699999999998,
      "x1": 567.1920000000001,
      "bottom": 192.59699999999998
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "cal strength but their dispersed type of formation. Size, players",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 194.59699999999998,
      "x1": 567.0049999999998,
      "bottom": 204.59699999999998
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "will soon realize, is the least important rating a unit has.",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 206.59699999999998,
      "x1": 538.87,
      "bottom": 216.59699999999998
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "The counter shape of a unit represents its frontage. A Phalanx",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 223.99699999999996,
      "x1": 566.988,
      "bottom": 233.99699999999996
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "in full array had a frontage of approximately 150 yards; thus,",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 235.99699999999996,
      "x1": 567.0029999999999,
      "bottom": 245.99699999999996
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "it occupies 2 hexes. A cavalry unit had a frontage of about 50+",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 247.99699999999996,
      "x1": 567.0029999999999,
      "bottom": 257.99699999999996
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "yards, or one hex.",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 259.99699999999996,
      "x1": 386.37,
      "bottom": 269.99699999999996
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "2.6 GAME LENGTH",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 280.571,
      "x1": 424.68,
      "bottom": 292.571
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "Generally, battles are fought until one side withdraws, so there",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 295.957,
      "x1": 567.0100000000001,
      "bottom": 305.957
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "is usually no need to keep track of how many turns have passed.",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 307.957,
      "x1": 566.9749999999999,
      "bottom": 317.957
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "A Game Turn Track has been provided to help track the timing",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 325.35699999999997,
      "x1": 567.0219999999998,
      "bottom": 335.35699999999997
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "of certain events (the entry of reinforcements, etc.) in some of",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 337.35699999999997,
      "x1": 567.0039999999999,
      "bottom": 347.35699999999997
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "the battles.",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 349.35699999999997,
      "x1": 358.33,
      "bottom": 359.35699999999997
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "HISTORICAL NOTE: Roman battles took somewhat longer",
      "x0": 319.5,
      "top": 368.36039999999997,
      "x1": 562.506,
      "bottom": 378.36039999999997
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "to complete than those of just 150 or so years previously.",
      "x0": 319.5,
      "top": 380.36039999999997,
      "x1": 562.5259999999998,
      "bottom": 390.36039999999997
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "Participants had developed a wide variety of tactical sys-",
      "x0": 319.5,
      "top": 392.36039999999997,
      "x1": 562.2859999999998,
      "bottom": 402.36039999999997
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "tems to counter those of their enemy. In addition, armor and",
      "x0": 319.5,
      "top": 404.36039999999997,
      "x1": 562.502,
      "bottom": 414.36039999999997
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "protection were lighter and more efficient, enabling soldiers",
      "x0": 319.5,
      "top": 416.36039999999997,
      "x1": 562.4999999999999,
      "bottom": 426.36039999999997
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "to fight longer. The result of all this was that casualties rose",
      "x0": 319.5,
      "top": 428.36039999999997,
      "x1": 562.499,
      "bottom": 438.36039999999997
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "precipitously, and battles lasted a great deal longer.",
      "x0": 319.5,
      "top": 440.36039999999997,
      "x1": 526.795,
      "bottom": 450.36039999999997
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "2.7 LATIN",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 465.43440000000004,
      "x1": 370.1148,
      "bottom": 477.43440000000004
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "We have tried to use appropriate Latin military terms, as appli-",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 480.8204,
      "x1": 567.0000000000001,
      "bottom": 490.8204
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "cable. Six years of hacking one’s way through Caesar’s Com-",
      "x0": 315.00000000000006,
      "top": 492.8204,
      "x1": 566.994,
      "bottom": 502.8204
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "mentaries finally came to some use. Memory, however, is a great",
      "x0": 315.00000000000006,
      "top": 504.8204,
      "x1": 567.1110000000001,
      "bottom": 514.8204000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "villain. I think we got most of the “endings” right; then again, if",
      "x0": 315.00000000000006,
      "top": 516.8204000000001,
      "x1": 567.0050000000001,
      "bottom": 526.8204000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "it came from the fifth declension, we probably “bluu” it.",
      "x0": 315.00000000000006,
      "top": 528.8204000000001,
      "x1": 539.69,
      "bottom": 538.8204000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "3.0 SEQUENCE OF PLAY",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 557.4764,
      "x1": 498.73120000000006,
      "bottom": 575.4764
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "Players activate each of their leaders in the order determined by",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 577.3604,
      "x1": 567.012,
      "bottom": 587.3604
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "their Initiative Rating. When a leader is activated, he issues orders",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 589.3604,
      "x1": 567.015,
      "bottom": 599.3604
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "which enable units to move and conduct combat. After all leaders",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 601.3604,
      "x1": 566.9159999999998,
      "bottom": 611.3604
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "are Finished, play proceeds to the Rout and Reload Phase, after",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 613.3604,
      "x1": 566.9899999999999,
      "bottom": 623.3604
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "which each player checks to see if his army withdraws.",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 625.3604,
      "x1": 535.5,
      "bottom": 635.3604
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
